{
  "markdown": "THE STATE OF OHIO.\nC HAMILTON COUNTY.\nss.\n\n\n83\nNo. 165\n\nPersonally appeared before me, the undersigned, JUDGE OF THE PROBATE COURT, within\nand for the County of Hamilton [William H Taft], who being\nduly sworn, deposeth and saith, that he is more than twenty-one years of age, and has no lawful\nwife living. And that [Helen L Herron]\nis more than eighteen years of age, and has no lawful husband living, that she is a resident of\nthe County of Hamilton aforesaid; and the said [William H Taft]\nfurther says, that said [Helen L Herron]\nand affiant are not of nearer relation to each other than that of second cousin, and that\nhe knows of no legal objection to the Marriage contemplated between them. And further\nthis deponent saith not.\n\n\n[SIGNED]\nSworn to and subscribed before me\nthis 19 day of June 1886\nHerman Hoebel\nPROBATE JUDGE.\nBy L Hauser Deputy Clerk.\nWm J Taft\n\n\nMARRIAGE RETURN.\n\n\nMARRIED, on the 19 day of June A.D. 1886\nWilliam H. Taft and Helen L. Herron\nby me a Minister of the Gospel\nA. Hogg\nTHE STATE OF OHIO\nMinister of the Gospel\n\n\n---\nTHE STATE OF OHIO\n\n\nTAFT MARRIAGE LICENSE\n\n\n<!-- doc_id=parse-01m7hkb36c4t2fyv15xe5g71sd -->",
